 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>Swing components</b> are ready-made GUI parts in <code>javax.swing</code> (names start with J) used to build user interfaces.</p><table><tr><th>Component</th><th>Use</th><th>Main methods / listener</th></tr><tr><td>JLabel</td><td>Show text/image</td><td>setText()</td></tr><tr><td>JButton</td><td>Clickable button</td><td>addActionListener()</td></tr><tr><td>JTextField</td><td>One-line input</td><td>getText(), setText()</td></tr><tr><td>JTextArea</td><td>Multi-line input</td><td>append()</td></tr><tr><td>JCheckBox</td><td>Select many options</td><td>isSelected(), ItemListener</td></tr><tr><td>JRadioButton</td><td>Select one (with ButtonGroup)</td><td>isSelected()</td></tr><tr><td>JComboBox</td><td>Dropdown list</td><td>getSelectedItem()</td></tr><tr><td>JList</td><td>List of items</td><td>getSelectedValue()</td></tr><tr><td>JPasswordField</td><td>Hidden text</td><td>getPassword()</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which component lets you choose only ONE option from a group?",
  "options": [
   "JCheckBox",
   "JRadioButton in a ButtonGroup",
   "JTextArea"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "One Group One Pick."
 }
}